```cpp
/*
Problem: 3Sum
Platform: LeetCode
Difficulty: Medium
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/3sum/

Approach:
First, sort the array.

Then use a for loop to fix the first number nums[i].
For every nums[i], use two pointers:
- left = i + 1
- right = n - 1

Calculate:
sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right]

If sum < 0:
    Move left forward because we need a bigger sum.

If sum > 0:
    Move right backward because we need a smaller sum.

If sum == 0:
    We found a valid triplet.
    Store it in the answer.
    Then move both pointers.

Duplicate Handling:
There can be duplicate numbers, but the answer must contain
unique triplets.

For the first number:
    if(i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1])
        continue;

This skips duplicate values of nums[i].

After finding a valid triplet:
    left++;
    right--;

Then skip duplicate values of left:
    while(left < right && nums[left] == nums[left - 1])
        left++;

This prevents adding the same triplet multiple times.

Time Complexity: O(n^2)
Space Complexity: O(1) extra space
(ignoring the output array and sorting implementation)

Important Tip:
3Sum is basically:

Sort
   ↓
Fix one number
   ↓
Use Two Pointers for the other two numbers
   ↓
Skip duplicates

Pattern:
3Sum = Sorting + For Loop + Two Pointers + Duplicate Handling

Mistake I Made:
I initially forgot that the loop should stop at n - 2
because we need three numbers:
nums[i], nums[left], nums[right].

Important:
    i < n - 2

Also, after finding a valid triplet, I must skip duplicates.
Otherwise, the same triplet can appear multiple times.

Key Learning:
Whenever a problem asks for unique combinations,
always think about how duplicates should be handled.

Pointer Movement:
sum < 0  -> left++
sum > 0  -> right--
sum == 0 -> store answer + move both pointers

*/
 
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> threeSum(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<vector<int>> ans;
        int n = nums.size();

        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {

            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1])
                continue;

            int left = i + 1;
            int right = n - 1;

            while (left < right) {

                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                if (sum < 0) {
                    left++;
                }
                else if (sum > 0) {
                    right--;
                }
                else {
                    ans.push_back({
                        nums[i],
                        nums[left],
                        nums[right]
                    });

                    left++;
                    right--;

                    while (left < right &&
                           nums[left] == nums[left - 1]) {
                        left++;
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
